# Introduction

This document provides a step-by-step guide for processing low-coverage whole-genome sequencing data from the spotted lanternfly (_Lycorma delicatula_). The pipeline involves SNP calling, linkage disequilibrium (LD) pruning, PCA analysis, demographic modeling, and heterozygosity estimation.

---

# Step 1: SNP Calling using ANGSD

```bash
#!/bin/bash -e

#SBATCH --nodes=1
#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=1
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=16
#SBATCH --time=128:00:00
#SBATCH --mem=64GB
#SBATCH --job-name=angsd_SNP_calling
#SBATCH --mail-type=BEGIN,END,FAIL
#SBATCH --mail-user=fm2371@nyu.edu
#SBATCH --output=slurm_%j.out

# Load necessary modules
module purge
module load angsd/intel/0.933 gsl/intel/2.6

# Define paths
